{"actor":"literature","data":{"citation":{"first_author":"Peter Adebayo Odesola","identifier":"doi:10.1101/2025.09.28.25336834","title":"Model uncertainty quantification: A post hoc calibration approach for heart disease prediction","year":2025},"claim":"Isotonic calibration significantly improves probability calibration metrics such as Brier score, Expected Calibration Error (ECE), and log loss for models including Random Forest, Naive Bayes, and SVM.","concepts":["calibration","random forest","isotonic regression","brier score"],"id":"E1","quote":"Isotonic calibration consistently improved probability quality for most models: random forest Brier from 0.007 to 0.002, ECE 0.051 to 0.011, log loss 0.056 to 0.012; naive Bayes Brier from 0.162 to 0.132, ECE 0.145 to 0.118, log loss 1.936 to 0.446; SVM ECE 0.086 to 0.044 and log loss 0.142 to 0.133.","stance":"supports"},"hash":"e36494d89cd5a97f3d619090434daa8331a69b44a1091051fe6bade264b83293","kind":"artefact","prev":"259797ee722b3d71ae2b90382587f132989290413e7592683bd2635c79f83d0b","seq":12,"stage":"evidence","ts":"2026-10-10T03:12:05.726+00:00"}
{"actor":"literature","data":{"citation":{"first_author":"Pedro G. Fonseca","identifier":"arxiv:1710.08901","title":"Calibration of Machine Learning Classifiers for Probability of Default Modelling","year":2017},"claim":"After applying isotonic regression for re-calibration, non-parametric models such as Random Forest and Gradient Boosting outperform logistic regression in terms of Brier score loss, indicating better probability calibration.","concepts":["calibration","random forest","isotonic regression","brier score"],"id":"E2","quote":"Using re-calibration, the non-parametric models are able to outperform the Logistic Regression on Brier Score Loss.","stance":"supports"},"hash":"3973c0239fe56b8402cff6d34791a4b61bb21929b5e4185ac4f4d68cdea2fd5b","kind":"artefact","prev":"e36494d89cd5a97f3d619090434daa8331a69b44a1091051fe6bade264b83293","seq":13,"stage":"evidence","ts":"2026-10-10T03:12:05.727+00:00"}
